<section class="band principles" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head center reveal">
            <p class="eyebrow centered">Private by design</p>
            <h2 id="principles-title">Your reading stays yours</h2>
            <p class="lead">Daily Quran collects nothing. What you read, and when, is between you and the page.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="principle-list">
            <li class="principle reveal">
                <span class="principle-icon">@Icon.NoAccount</span>
                <h3>No account</h3>
                <p>Open the app and read. There is nothing to sign up for and nothing to sign in to.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="principle reveal">
                <span class="principle-icon">@Icon.EyeOff</span>
                <h3>No ads, no tracking</h3>
                <p>No advertising, no analytics, no crash reporting. On Android the app does not even have permission to use the internet.</p>
            </li>
            <li class="principle reveal">
                <span class="principle-icon">@Icon.Phone</span>
                <h3>On your phone, offline</h3>
                <p>Your place, plans, favourites and reading time stay on your device, and the whole Qur’an reads without a connection.</p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>
